    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> be three non zero vectors such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>(</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> be a vector such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>)</mo><mo>&#183;</mo><mo>(</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></math> is equal to",
